# Docker sends the whole build context up front, so an unignored target/ (tens
# of gigabytes here) looks like a build that hangs before its first layer.
#
# Exclude by size, and only what the build cannot reach. Everything the crate
# embeds has to stay: `assets/` (themes via include_str!, fonts via
# include_bytes!), `WIZARD.md` (the charter, compiled into the system prompt),
# `tests/fixtures/` (one recorded SSE stream a unit test embeds), and
# `wizard-release.pub`. Dropping `assets/` here once cost a build that failed
# 118 seconds in on `couldn't read src/../assets/themes/grok.toml`.
target/
target-glibc/
.git/
demo/
jobs/
